        "v": "For underwriting, the KYC provider is another company on another framework. Its agent asks clarifying questions and takes hours to complete a task. That is stateful, opaque, and multi-turn, so it is an A2A peer. The bank's agent reads the provider's Agent Card, opens a Task, and receives Artifacts as documents arrive. The bank's own underwriting steps stay as subagents inside its Agent SDK application. [7][8][9]"
